            <span class="lvg-truth-chapters__label">
              Chapter five
            </span>
          

          
            <h2>
              Renewal runs on the skin's clock,<br>
not on a marketing one.
            </h2>
          

          

            <div class="lvg-truth-chapters__two">

              
                <div>
                  <p>New cells have to form, mature and reach the surface. That takes the time it takes, and no amount of ambition compresses it. Meaningful visible improvement needs consistency across several renewal cycles — which is why this brand says seventy-five days, and does not say seven.</p>
                </div>
              

              
                <div>
                  <p>Overnight results and week-long transformations were not invented by skin biology. They were invented by the thing described on the previous page, and they are a large part of why the loop turns as fast as it does.</p>
                </div>
              

            </div>

          

        </div>


        

        

          
          

          

          


          

